## 5. Forbidden actions (DAG edges)

1. M4-T7 recorded: G1 restore (`rehearsal_bot_pg15`) is **`0111`**. `subscriptions.remnawave_id` **3170/3173** (G6). C2C/FA/Toman/wholesale ported; **G8 PASS** (M6-T4, isolated chat fp `0fcbb8097f77ea8b`). Do not commit a full `alembic revision --autogenerate` (would create deferred tables and drop C2C/wholesale). Never `alembic upgrade` / `stamp` sandbox `remnabot1_postgres_data` (still upstream `0110`) with the grafted graph. `rehearsal_bot` polling is authorized after M6-T4.
2. Never `docker compose up` / restore against production or legacy volumes (`bot-remnawave_postgres_data`, `remnawave-db-data`, etc.). Rehearsal uses only `rehearsal_*` / `cutover_*` names.
3. Never start the production-token bot until the old production bot is stopped (M8).
4. Never apply archived remnabot1 upstream `0088–0110` (now under `docs/superpowers/reference/upstream-alembic-0088-0110/`) to a remnabot-lineage `0103` database.
5. Never leave production Remnawave `nodes` rows in a second live panel (E8). After restoring a RW dump, empty `nodes` before leaving `rehearsal_rw` running. Do not attach a production node or copy production node keys. A live node is not required for M4. Isolated dummy only if a later named batch asks (`rw-rehearsal.rookari.com` → this host → `127.0.0.1:3100`).

Set `SKIP_MIGRATION=true` on sandbox `remnawave_bot` if it must restart (DB is still `0110`).

